16.21.m:
Go, worship the lord of the gods through fierce austerity;
praising the god of the lords of gods, make yourself spotless. / By his swift granting of boons, you will attain an excellent form.
Thus ends the twenty-first chapter, entitled 'Description of the Instruction on Worshipping Śiva to Remove the Diseases of Consumption and Leprosy of the Moon Afflicted with Consumption Born of His Curse by Dakṣa, in the Context of the Origin of Someśvara', in the first [part], Prabhāsakṣetramāhātmya, of the seventh Prabhāsakhaṇḍa in the glorious Skanda Mahāpurāṇa, a collection of eighty-one thousand [verses].
